    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.33,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.8,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 1.22 from 6 h to 18 h. Dilutions of the 18 h aliquot, scaled back up, read higher than that. A 10x dilution gave 0.135 (two replicates, 0.1325 and 0.1375), which scales to about 1.35. A 40x dilution gave 0.0324, which scales to about 1.30 but is noisier. Both are above 1.22, so the undiluted reader is slightly non-linear at high density and the plateau understates biomass by roughly 8-10%. The effect is modest and the evidence is not overwhelming. The 10x result is the more precise one, and it is clearly above the undiluted value."
  },
